# An error exit from inside the GUI: gui023's zip has a file named
# BAD*NAME.TXT, which NextZXOS cannot create, so the install ends .spun with
# "Cannot create a file" (BANK_packages/install.c). BASIC's screen must be
# back before that message is printed, so the message and the lines BASIC
# printed before .spun show on it, and nothing of the GUI or the browser
# does. Without ON ERROR the autoexec would end at the error and NextZXOS
# would show its menu. The handler jumps to line 60, the loop that never
# ends, so the screen stays as it is: BASIC prints no report for a trapped
# error, and the PRINT of line 50 runs only if .spun returns without an
# error, which would put SPUNNOERROR on row 3 and fail the ula check of
# mame-install.sh. NextZXOS fetches $0000 once when a handler catches the
# error of a dot command, with BASIC at the line of that command, and the
# harness logs it as a "reset" line, so this scenario has no noreset;
# mame-install.sh fails it on a "machine reset" line in mame.log instead.
# gui023 is third in the list.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
autostart PRINT "SPUNBEFORE1": PRINT "SPUNBEFORE2"
autostart ON ERROR GO TO 60
autostart .spun -p @PORT@
autostart PRINT "SPUNNOERROR"
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 48
mouse 2 move 128 128
key 16 {DOWN}
key 16.5 {DOWN}
key 17 {ENTER}
mouse 21.5 move 64 12
@POINTER 22 96 244
mouse 22.2 press left
mouse 22.3 release left
key 26.5 6
key 28.5 {ENTER}
key 30.5 {SPACE}
key 33.5 i
dump 46.5 0x4000 6912 ula-end
snap 32.5 34 35.5 46.5
screen 47 SPUNBEFORE1
screen 47 SPUNBEFORE2
screen 47 Cannot create a file
